> thinking initially of the question "Do you like (at least one of, or
> possibly other similar alternatives to) coffee or tea?" .i mi djuno (there
> should absolutely be a fi here! ki'e selpa'i) lo xamgu mutce/xamgu (I'd
> imagine informal Lojban would lend itself really well to reduplication)
> kafyzai .i mi tervecnu (selpa'i cu drani) tezu'e ko pinxe}
>
>
> t'o-n xenru l m-xlacus :( ; r l'a n-slabu ri'a r n-ri'i ;je ti-fnx kargu
> ;je m-c-c'o jdn-sl-nabmi 666
> {.i ta'onai [mi] xenru lo mi xlacu'u .uinai .i ri la'a na slabu [do] ri'a
> [do] na lifri .ije ti fonxa cu kargu .ije mi caca'o (tsani cu drani) jdini
> selnabmi}
> (Hoo boy, this got complicated. A gloss of what I attempted: "Anyway,
> sorry for my sloppy speaking (probably needed nu). :( It's probably not
> familiar to you, because you haven't had much experience with it. Also,
> this phone is expensive. Also also, I've been having money problems, rofl."
