> way. Finally, c and c'o are both context dependent: clearly coi and co'o at
> endpoints of conversation, but ca and ca'o before selbri and connected with
> hyphens.)
>
>
> l m-1f-b-sispe'i-d bu'u l vij-tcan
> {.i le mi patfu ba sispe'i do bu'u le vijytcana (Mostly I was looking for
> more ways to use number-rebus. See also: 2'i, 5'o, 8nxo, 9'a etc, now that
> I think of it.)}
>
>
> g'e "FIhI LA JBOGU'E" 66
> {.i ge'e lu fi'i la jbogu'e li'u .u'i (Was going for "So I guess, WELCOME
